This directory vendors the Python implementation of the Industrial Benchmark.

Source: https://github.com/siemens/industrialbenchmark, directory
`industrial_benchmark_python/` (commit afeed69, 2022-12-06).
Authors: Stefan Depeweg and Alexander Hentschel (Siemens AG); benchmark paper:
Hein et al., "A Benchmark Environment Motivated by Industrial Control
Problems", IEEE SSCI 2017 (arXiv:1709.09480).
Licensed under the MIT License, as stated in the header of every vendored
file; see LICENSE. (The repository's top-level LICENCE.txt is Apache-2.0 and
covers the Java implementation.)

Vendored files: `__init__.py`, `IDS.py`, `EffectiveAction.py`, and
`goldstone/`. Not vendored: `IBGym.py` (depends on the old `gym` package; the
projeto-rl adapter `projeto_rl/envs/industrial_benchmark.py` reproduces the discrete
action table and the `reward_type="classic"` reward it uses), tests, examples,
and the Java implementation.

Local modifications to `IDS.py`:
- Random numbers: the constructor takes a `numpy.random.Generator` (`rng`, now
  the first argument) and every draw uses it; the original seeded and drew
  from numpy's global random state (`np.random.seed`, `np.random.rand`, ...).
  The `inital_seed` argument was removed.
- `np.float(...)`, removed in NumPy 1.24, is replaced by `float(...)`.
No other file was changed.
